// random — Random number generators and sampling utilities
//
// Fast, high-quality PRNGs and distribution samplers for scientific computing.
// The xoshiro module uses Sounio's Prob effect to make randomness visible at the type level.
//
// Submodules:
//   rng           — SplitMix64 (seeding), PCG64 (default), Xoshiro256++ (fast)
//   xoshiro       — Xoshiro256** with Prob effect: uniform, normal, exponential, bernoulli, shuffle
//   distributions — Sample from Uniform, Normal, LogNormal, Exponential, Gamma, Beta, Poisson
//   sampling      — Weighted selection, shuffle, bootstrap resampling, PK variability
//   park_miller   — Single-state Park-Miller LCG for PBPK / Monte Carlo (see note below)
//
// !! 2026-05-16 RNG GUIDANCE !!
// PCG64 in `distributions.sio` and `rng.sio` is currently broken under the
// pinned souc binary — see the deprecation header in `distributions.sio` for
// the dual-cause analysis from Sounio-Pure dispatch R.2.1. For PBPK / Monte
// Carlo work and any thesis-bound scientific output, use the new
// `park_miller` submodule. Quality is adequate for biological simulation
// (n ≪ 10^8 samples per cohort); see park_miller.sio for full caveats.

// rng — types: SplitMix64, Pcg64, RngXoshiro256
// Key fns: splitmix64_new, splitmix64_next,
//   pcg64_new, pcg64_next_i64, pcg64_next_f64, pcg64_next_bool, pcg64_bounded,
//   xoshiro256_new, xoshiro256_next_i64, xoshiro256_next_f64

// xoshiro — types: Xoshiro256
// Key fns: xoshiro_seed, uniform, uniform_range, normal, standard_normal,
//   exponential, bernoulli, discrete_uniform, shuffle_f64

// distributions — types: Uniform, Normal, LogNormal, Exponential, Gamma, Beta, Poisson
// Key fns: uniform_sample, normal_sample, lognormal_sample, exponential_sample,
//   gamma_sample, beta_sample, poisson_sample

// sampling — Key fns: sample_normal, sample_index, sample_one_f64, sample_one_i64,
//   sample_weighted_index, smp_shuffle_f64, shuffle_i64, resample_f64
